BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Wild Benches of Hope Exhibit
DTSTART:20260121T000000
DTEND:20260121T020000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:7334d23679e15846b695ce8273b3b3@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Wild Benches of Hope is a free\, public art exhibition by 
 internationally acclaimed artists Gillie and Marc\, on view at Faneuil Hal
 l Marketplace from January 2026 through January 2027. The interactive inst
 allation features three large-scale bronze benches - The Reading Bench\, T
 he Green Bench\, and The Teatime Bench - where visitors can sit alongside 
 the artists’ beloved characters\, Rabbitwoman and Dogman\, and endangere
 d animals including a giraffe\, hippo\, and elephant. Designed for all age
 s\, the sculptures invite moments of curiosity\, imagination\, and connect
 ion during a visit to the Marketplace. Presented in partnership with Zoo N
 ew England\, the exhibition introduces families to important conservation 
 themes in an approachable\, engaging way - encouraging visitors to slow do
 wn\, learn together\, and feel inspired to protect wildlife near and far. 
 Donate to Zoo New England today! This marks a continuation of Faneuil Hall
  Marketplace’s new\, long-term arts initiative aimed to connect Boston r
 esidents and visitors to a diverse range of public art.\n\nSources: Meet B
 oston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-wild-benches-of-ho
 pe-exhibit/88911/
LOCATION:Faneuil Hall Marketplace\, 4 South Market Street 3rd Floor\, Bost
 on\, MA\, 02109
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-wild-benches-of-hope-exhibit/8891
 1/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:To My Best Friend
DTSTART:20260123T000000
DTEND:20260123T020000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:d349c4f1ef27d7d9be2143d1426663@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:To My Best Friend c elebrates art and artists\, reflecting the
  ICA’s history of presenting leading contemporary voices and the past tw
 o decades of building a dynamic collection. As the ICA Collection has grow
 n to more than 400 works—spanning painting\, sculpture\, photography\, i
 nstallation\, and more—longtime friends and supporters Fotene Demoulas a
 nd Tom Coté have played an essential role in shaping its direction. Their
  sustained focus on historically underrepresented and women artists at all
  stages of their careers reflects a deep engagement with the ICA and a sha
 red belief in contemporary art’s capacity to build community and broaden
  visibility for diverse perspectives. Drawing from more than 50 artworks D
 emoulas and Coté have helped bring into the ICA Collection\, this exhibit
 ion highlights a consistent interest in formal and material experimentatio
 n through works by Laura Owens\, Njideka Akunyili Crosby\, Olga de Amaral
 \, and Sarah Sze\, among others\, and a recognition of the singular insigh
 ts artists offer the world. Together\, these works honor the relationships
  that have defined the ICA throughout its 90-year history\, and continue t
 o inspire its future\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meet
 boston.com/event/to-my-best-friend/88583/
LOCATION:Institute of Contemporary Art\, 25 Harbor Shore Drive\, Boston\, 
 MA\, 02210
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/to-my-best-friend/88583/
END:VEVENT
