BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Harvard Square French Fry & Food Pairings Tour
DTSTART:20260426T000000
DTEND:20260426T020000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:04001334fa59e5f1126212844bb61c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:On this exciting food tour\, great for everyone from grad stud
 ents to kids to adults\, we sample the best french fries in Harvard Square
  and pair them with yummy (non-alcoholic) drinks. You’ll hear fun storie
 s about the French Fry Wars of the 20th Century and hilarious tales of Har
 vard Square lore. What to Expect Stroll the famous Harvard Square with us 
 together with a friendly guide. Enjoy Mr. Bartley’s famous sweet potato 
 fries paired with the original raspberry lime rickey. Pass the Widener Lib
 rary and Harvard Yard and relax in greek hospitality\, enjoying greek frie
 s and peach lemonade at Saloniki. Visit the Harvard Lampoon building and p
 ass the Harvard Faculty Club as well as storied buildings from the cobbles
 tone streets. End your tour with a delicious sample of a crazy ice cream f
 rappe and fantastically flavored hand-cut fry wedges. Celebrate the infamo
 us French Fry Wars of the late 20th Century\, and rub elbows with all kind
 s in this eclectic and fun neighborhood. You’ll laugh\, have a blast\, a
 nd enjoy delicious eats on this hilarious Harvard Square adventure! Note: 
 Sample itinerary is subject to change based on availability. Meet Meet in 
 front of BARTLEY’S BURGER COTTAGE (1246 Massachusetts Avenue\, Cambridge
 )\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/ha
 rvard-square-french-fry-%26-food-pairings-tour/90314/
LOCATION:Off The Beaten Path Food Tours\, Bartley's Burger Cottage 1246 Ma
 ssachusetts Avenue\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02116
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/harvard-square-french-fry-%26-food-pa
 irings-tour/90314/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Daily Guided and Self-Guided Tours
DTSTART:20260428T000000
DTEND:20261116T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:458a058c6e93187ad044b7409bd901@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Hammond Castle Museum welcomes guests to tour the many rooms o
 f the home and laboratory of John Hays Hammond Jr.\, renowned as one of th
 e most prolific American inventors of the 20th century and famously known 
 as the Father of Radio Control. Throughout the 2026 season guests can also
  enjoy a completely updated Invention Room\, showcasing exciting new persp
 ectives on Hammond’s work as a scientist\, inventor and engineer\, as we
 ll as a brand-new set of rotating exhibits\, including “Inside the Farad
 ay Cage: The Science of Things that Aren’t So” in the spring and summe
 r and “Brave Too Much: The Legend of John Coffee Hays” in the fall and
  winter. We offer two options for daily admission: Guided and Self-Guided 
 tours. Guided Tours: Led by a member of Hammond Castle Museum’s talented
  tours staff\, Guided Tours of the Museum last approximately 35-40 minutes
  and cover basic information about the history of the building and its inh
 abitants. Major areas covered by the tour staff include parts of the forme
 r Laboratory\, the vast Great Hall\, and the breathtaking Courtyard. After
  the guided portion of the tour\, visitors may explore the many smaller ro
 oms and exhibit spaces in the former Hammond residence. Self-Guided Tours:
  Experience Hammond Castle Museum at your own pace with our flexible arriv
 al times for Self-Guided Tours! Your ticket grants you entry anytime withi
 n the Morning or Afternoon session times\, based upon your selection\, ens
 uring you can arrive stress-free and enjoy your visit to the fullest. Morn
 ing Session: 9:00 am – 11:45 am Afternoon Session: 11:45 am – 2:30 pm 
 Please note: the last entrance into the Museum is at 2:45 pm sharp. The Mu
 seum and Grounds close promptly at 3:30 pm. We recommend planning at least
  60 minutes to explore the grounds and interior galleries of the Museum. T
 he Hammond Castle Museum is a historic landmark built in the late 1920s\, 
 and as such is not handicapped accessible and presents challenges for visi
 tors with mobility impairments\, as it features numerous stairs. LEARN MOR
 E / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetbosto
 n.com/event/daily-guided-and-self-guided-tours/89825/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/daily-guided-and-self-guided-tours/89
 825/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
