SUMMARY:Self-Guided Walking Tour: Harvard & the American Revolution
DTSTART:20260610T000000
DTEND:20260610T020000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:cfda55735807a7fd7ec5ea8e0d729d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In honor of 2026 marking the 250th anniversary of the United S
 tates Declaration of Independence and the founding of the United States\, 
 we invite you to take part in a free\, self-guided walking tour highlighti
 ng historic Revolutionary Era sites in and around Harvard University. The 
 tour features 16 stops beginning at the Smith Campus Center and continuing
  through Harvard Yard and explores the role that Harvard affiliates had in
  shaping the nation’s path to independence\, and how the Harvard campus 
 transformed and operated between 1775-1776. Download the app on iOS and An
 droid devices or explore the desktop experience.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\n
 Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/self-guided-walking-tour%3a-h
 arvard-%26-the-american-revolution/90911/
LOCATION:Harvard University\, Harvard University Harvard Square\, Cambridg
 e\, MA
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/self-guided-walking-tour%3a-harvard-%
 26-the-american-revolution/90911/
END:VEVENT
