BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The American Five
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260618
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260619
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:78e5aca03862f2810624864f57bd98@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Written by Chess Jakobs\, The American Five explores pivotal m
 oments in the lives of Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.\, Coretta Scott King\, B
 ayard Rustin\, Stanley Levison and Clarence B. Jones during the height of 
 the Civil Rights Movement. Set in the tense days leading up to the March o
 n Washington\, the play examines the strategy\, collaboration and moral co
 nviction behind one of the most consequential events in American history. 
 Developed through workshops at Ford’s Theatre and the University of Mich
 igan and premiering at Ford’s Theatre in September 2025\, this regional 
 premiere highlights themes of nonviolence\, leadership and personal sacrif
 ice while illuminating the immense pressure facing those who stood at the 
 forefront of change. In the face of government surveillance\, intimidation
 \, arrests and constant threats\, these five figures forged a coalition gr
 ounded in trust\, intellect and unwavering belief in justice.\n\nSources: 
 The Berkshires\nEvent page: https://berkshires.org/events-old/the-american
 -five/
LOCATION:Unicorn Theatre\, 6 East Street\, Stockbridge\, MA\, 01262
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/the-american-five/
END:VEVENT
