DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:556fcc38a748305c09adf011553241@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Chinatown is a neighborhood shaped by generations of artists\,
  organizers\, business owners\, and residents who have worked together to 
 create a vibrant and dignified home for immigrant and working-class commun
 ities. This exhibition celebrates the collective effort behind the Boston 
 Chinatown Cultural Plan\, a community-driven vision developed through coll
 aboration among local Chinatown organizations\, the Metropolitan Area Plan
 ning Council\, and the City of Boston. Through eight past and ongoing proj
 ects led by four collaborating organizations\, the exhibition offers a beh
 ind-the-scenes look at how cultural planning can strengthen community conn
 ections\, celebrate Boston Chinatown’s rich history\, and imagine its fu
 ture. Featured projects are presented by Asian Community Development Corpo
 ration\, Chinatown Community Land Trust\, Pao Arts Center\, and the Rose K
 ennedy Greenway Conservancy.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://
 www.meetboston.com/event/tracing-our-footprints-carving-chinatowns-future/
 91443/
LOCATION:Pao Arts Center\, Pao Arts Center 99 Albany Street\, Boston\, MA
 \, 02111
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/tracing-our-footprints-carving-chinat
 owns-future/91443/
END:VEVENT
