DESCRIPTION:Explore how music unites and inspires worshipers\, with histor
 y\, visuals\, and artifacts taking us from the earliest services in the ch
 urch to a worldwide virtual hymn sing. Explore the life\, ideas\, and achi
 evements of Mary Baker Eddy\, the Discoverer and Founder of Christian Scie
 nce—a pioneer whose work touched the fields of religion\, health\, and j
 ournalism. The fourth-floor Research Room is open to the public Monday to 
 Thursday from 11:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. research@mbelibrary.org 617-450-7218
  “May those who discourse music to-day\, sing as the angels heaven’s s
 ymphonies that come to earth.” (Mary Baker Eddy to First Church of Chris
 t\, Scientist\, Concord\, New Hampshire\, March 30\, 1902)\n\nSources: Mee
 t Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/music-in-the-christ
 ian-science-tradition/92871/
