BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maverick Kings: Three Visionary Pharaohs of Egypt’s Golden Age
DTSTART:20260906T000000
DTEND:20261206T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:2d34b8166e2c8d18a3b1d063498f0d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Drawing primarily from the MFA’s extensive collection of anc
 ient Egyptian art\, one of the largest and most important in the world\, 
 “Maverick Kings” explores the lives and legacies of dynamic monarchs t
 hrough their art and own words. Visitors can see major monuments to Hatshe
 psut\, including the only royal sarcophagus from the 18th Dynasty outside 
 of Egypt\; large statues of deities in animal form\, a style characteristi
 c of Amenhotep III’s reign\, such as a nearly six-foot-tall statue of a 
 falcon\; and a sculpted portrait of Akhenaten’s son\, Tutankhamen (reign
 ed about 1332–1323 BCE)\, who restored the cults of the old gods. Togeth
 er these objects reveal how\, just as we fashion public personas for our o
 wn ends today\, these three pharaohs created and used their own images to 
 achieve and retain political power. The exhibition also includes objects o
 n loan from the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York\, the Egyptian Muse
 um in Berlin\, the Cleveland Museum of Art\, and the Kimbell Art Museum in
  Fort Worth\, Texas. It ends with contemporary art by Awol Erizku and othe
 rs that exemplifies the perennial influence and appeal of ancient Egyptian
  imagery. See It with a Ticket Everyone needs a timed-entry ticket to see 
 the exhibition\, including members—reserve yours to guarantee entry. Don
 ’t forget\, exhibition tickets include general admission to the Museum! 
 LEARN MORE/ GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.m
 eetboston.com/event/maverick-kings%3a-three-visionary-pharaohs-of-egypt%e2
 %80%99s-golden-age/92840/
LOCATION:Museum of Fine Arts\, Boston\, 465 Huntington Avenue\, Boston\, M
 A\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/maverick-kings%3a-three-visionary-pha
 raohs-of-egypt%e2%80%99s-golden-age/92840/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queens\, Gods\, and Devotees: Selections from the Petrucci Family 
 Foundation Collection of African American Art
DTSTART:20260908T000000
DTEND:20261124T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:81090a711f3b61b36a07112fc00bc5@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:PRESENTED BY THE IRIS & B. GERALD CANTOR ART GALLERY Featuring
  over 30 paintings\, sculptures\, photographs\, prints\, and fiber works f
 rom c. 1900 to the present\, Queens\, Gods\, and Devotees foregrounds eart
 hly and divine greatness\, and their associated devotional objects and rit
 ual practices. Many of these images of exalted figures and concepts relate
 d to spirituality and worship are specific to the Black American experienc
 e\, or are re-imagined in a Black cultural context. References to Greek my
 thology\, the Judeo-Christian tradition\, ancient cultures and traditional
  African spiritual practices appear alongside one another. The exhibition 
 includes work by celebrated artists including Romare Bearden\, Henry Ossaw
 a Tanner\, Richmond Barthé\, John Biggers\, Willie Cole\, Shinique Smith
 \, Tawny Chatmon\, Imo Nse Imeh and Sharif Bey\, among others. Selections 
 in Queens\, Gods\, and Devotees are drawn entirely from the Petrucci Famil
 y Foundation Collection of African American Art. The PFF Collection is a t
 argeted initiative to bring focus to the full range of African American vi
 sual creativity and its essential place in the history and discourse of Am
 erican Art. As part of a growing and thoughtful dialogue about the African
  American experience through art\, the PFF Collection seeks to visually re
 present a cross-section of themes that speak not only to the African Ameri
 can community\, but also the broader American community. Curated by Susann
 a W. Gold\, Ph.D. EXHIBITION EVENTS Opening Reception | Thursday\, Septemb
 er 17 | 5:30 PM | Cantor Art Gallery Artist Talk: Imo Nse Imeh\, Feeding t
 he Veins of the Earth | Thursday\, October 1 | 4:30 PM at the Rehm Library
  (3rd Floor\, Smith Hall) LOCATION & HOURS The Cantor Art Gallery is locat
 ed on the third floor of The Prior Performing Arts Center. Admission is fr
 ee and open to the public. Regular Hours: Sunday closed Monday by appointm
 ent only Tuesday 10am-5pm Wednesday 10am-5pm Thursday 10am-5pm Friday 10am
 -5pm Saturday 12pm-5pm VISITOR PARKING REGISTRATION Holy Cross is pleased 
 to offer free\, nearby parking in the Hogan parking lots on the College’
 s Upper Campus for all Prior Performing Arts Center & Cantor Art Gallery v
 isitors during open hours and during public events & presentations. Please
  be advised that\, while visitor parking in these lots is free\, registrat
 ion is required for all guests in order to avoid ticketing or towing. Visi
 t The Prior's website to learn more about visitor parking and access the p
 arking registration form.\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEven
 t page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/queens-gods-and-devotees%3
 a-selections-from-the-petrucci-family-foundation-collection-of-african-ame
 rican-art/30821/
LOCATION:Prior Performing Arts Center\, 1 College St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 0
 1610
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/queens-gods-and-devotees%3a-se
 lections-from-the-petrucci-family-foundation-collection-of-african-america
 n-art/30821/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Marathon Run Experience
DTSTART:20260908T000000
DTEND:20260908T020000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:e7901a8fb95f06422c74370a0509e7@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Ready to experience Boston from a runner's perspective? Join u
 s for this 3.6-mile guided running tour through the city's most iconic lan
 dmarks\, all while soaking in the rich history and vibrant energy that mak
 e Boston such a unique place to explore. You'll hit must-see spots—Bosto
 n Common\, the Boston Public Garden\, and Copley Square\, while passing by
  picturesque views along the Charles River Esplanade\, Beacon Hill\, and t
 he world-famous Back Bay. Along the way\, we’ll make stops at scenic spo
 ts for photo ops and quick stretch breaks—perfect for both seasoned runn
 ers and those looking to enjoy the sights at a comfortable pace. Your guid
 e will share fascinating stories about the city’s history and culture\, 
 from the moments that shaped Boston into the powerhouse it is today to the
  quirky details you won’t find in a guidebook. Whether you're a local or
  a first-time visitor\, you’ll finish this run with a deeper appreciatio
 n of Boston's charm. LEARN MORE / BOOK A TOUR\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEve
 nt page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-marathon-run-experience/8838
 6/
LOCATION:City Fit Tours\, Boston Common 139 Tremont Street\, Boston\, MA\,
  10075
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-marathon-run-experience/88386/
END:VEVENT
