BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sidelights
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20261005T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:edb1c60648c7405bf707267195514b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Harold Stevens Gallery presents “ Sidelights: An Immersive M
 ultimedia Installation” by Matthew Wasser. What happens when a painting 
 becomes a portal—and the viewer becomes part of the artwork? In Sideligh
 ts\, Worcester multimedia artist Matthew Wasser transforms the Harold Stev
 ens Gallery into an immersive environment where projection\, light\, sound
 \, and movement converge to blur the boundaries between physical and virtu
 al space. The installation combines multiple projectors\, interactive vide
 o technology\, ambient sound\, and subtle recitations from Shakespeare to 
 create a space that is both contemplative and playful. Visitors are encour
 aged to interact and explore the possibilities in this evolving visual lan
 dscape. Wasser is an internationally known video and media artist. His wor
 k includes\, lighting design for theatre\, dance\, and opera productions a
 cross the United States and abroad. A recent MFA graduate from Clark Unive
 rsity/Becker School of Design and Technology and is presently employed at 
 the Boston Museum of Science. This program is supported in part by a grant
  from the Worcester Arts Council\, a local agency\, which is supported by 
 the Mass Cultural Council\, a state agency.\n\nSources: Discover Central M
 assachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/sideligh
 ts/30968/
LOCATION:Harold Stevens Gallery at WCUW\, 910 Main St\, Worcester\, MA\, 0
 1610
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/sidelights/30968/
END:VEVENT
