BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Fall of the House of Usher
DTSTART:20260930T000000
DTEND:20261025T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:76ccb6b17f38b8d991353e46f09964@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Fall of the House of Usher Written by Gip Hoppe Directed b
 y James P. Byrne Set Design by Ryan McGettigan Costume Design by Cat Perry
  Lighting Design by John Malinowski Sound Design & Music by J Hagenbuckle 
 Stage Manager Kaleigh Mason Performances will be held in Cape Rep’s Indo
 or Theater September 30 - October 25\, Wednesday - Saturday at 7:30 pm\, S
 unday at 2 pm\; additional matinees Saturday 10/10\, 10/17 and 10/24 at 2:
 00 pm. Tickets are $40\, $30 for 35 and under. Student Rush 1/2 price at t
 he door day of show and Pay-What-You-Like the first Friday 10/02. Don’t 
 miss Cape Cod Chronicle Night in the Barn on Thursday\, October 1\, 6:30 p
 m. Call the box office or see us online at caperep.org for reservations an
 d information. Cape Rep Indoor Theater\, North Side Route 6A E. Brewster\,
  508.896.1888 or www.caperep.org. Over the top drama\, exaggerated emotion
 s\, high stakes\, sensational situations…Gip’s wildly popular adaptati
 on of this Edgar Allan Poe short story was a huge hit in 1990. Gip passed 
 away recently and his creative influence extended to many\, many artists i
 n Lower Cape theater. We have chosen to mount this production to honor Gip
 ’s early work\, and incredibly fertile creative energy. James P. Byrne w
 ill direct this dramatic production that is a designer’s dream and we ha
 ve the dream team of designers with J Hagebuckle’s original music\, Ryan
  McGettigan’s scenic design\, Cat Perry on costume design\, John Malinow
 ski’s lighting. Stage manager Kaleigh Mason’s expertise helps bring ev
 ery moment seamlessly to the stage. The cast features Nathaniel Hall Taylo
 r\, Mike Steers\, Jade Schuyler\, Ari Lew\, Colin Bourget\, Jefferson Thom
 as\, Jenn Pina\, Jack Kerig\, and Julie Allen Hamilton. All performances w
 ill be in Cape Rep’s Indoor Theater\, 3299 Main Street\, Brewster. New t
 his season\, more matinees! You asked\, we listened! We have added more ma
 tinees across the season. Check each show’s schedule for exact dates! Fo
 r further information or to purchase tickets\, contact the box office at 5
 08.896.1888 or online at www.caperep.org.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEv
 ent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/the-fall-of-the-house-of-us
 her/52417/
LOCATION:Cape Rep Theatre\, 3299 Route 6A PO Box 1305\, East Brewster\, MA
 \, 02631
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/the-fall-of-the-house-of-usher/52
 417/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOUNCERS
DTSTART:20261001T000000
DTEND:20261024T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:a3f35cd370bfdd013c3ea6d41ad2ff@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Visual City LLC and Suffolk University’s Modern Theatre pres
 ent BOUNCERS by John Godber Directed by Bill Doncaster We welcome you to a
  vision of British urban night-life To stag nights and he-do’s\, to drun
 ken crying girls and gallons of booze We present to you BOUNCERS\, by John
  Godber\, among the most frequently produced plays in the UK\, and named b
 y the National Theatre as one of the "Plays of the Century". It’s a fast
 -paced romp dramatizing the escapades of young lads and lasses at a hard d
 rinking disco where "there's sex in the air\, and the hunt is on”. Four 
 bouncers endeavor to illustrate the madness of the throngs that converge o
 n the discoteque -- embodying a whirlwind of characters\, male and female 
 -- in the pulsating debauchery of a typical Friday night. October 1 - 24\,
  2026 | Thurs\, Fri\, & Sat\, at 8:00 PM Modern Theatre Lobby (and bar!) a
 t 7:00 PM LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: ht
 tps://www.meetboston.com/event/bouncers/93305/
LOCATION:The Modern Theatre at Suffolk University\, The Modern Theatre at 
 Suffolk University 525 Washington Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02111
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/bouncers/93305/
