SUMMARY:Museums on Us from Bank of America
DTSTART:20261003T000000
DTEND:20261004T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:5fca7b202e48bf8daa38f0ad4e0e53@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The first weekend of every month\, Bank of America's monthly "
 Museums on Us" program offers free admission to a number of Boston's most 
 prestigious museums. The nationwide program is available to all Bank of Am
 erica\, Merrill\, and Bank of America Private Bank cardholders\, and opens
  up more than 225 of the nation's most prominent cultural institutions in 
 35 states. In Central and Western Massachusetts\, the participating museum
 s are: • EcoTarium\, Worcester Featured Exhibit: "Big League fun" • Th
 e Mount\, Edith Wharton's home in Lenox: Grounds are open year round • O
 rchard House\, Louisa May Alcott's home in Concord. From April - October 2
 026 • Springfield Museums Featured Exhibit: "Legacies of Surrealism: Wor
 ks from the Museo de Arte de Ponce" • Fitchburg Art Museum: New Exhibit:
  "Elisa H. Hamilton: Heirlooms" Bank of America offers this benefit to pro
 mote greater cultural understanding\, expand accessibility to the arts\, a
 nd strengthen communities. Upon arriving at a participating institution\, 
 customers need only present their Bank of America\, Merrill or Bank of Ame
 rica Private Bank credit or debit card along with a photo ID to gain free 
 general admission for themselves.\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachuset
 ts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/museums-on-us-from
 -bank-of-america/30994/
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/museums-on-us-from-bank-of-ame
 rica/30994/
END:VEVENT
