BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shoebert’s Unfinished Journey
DTSTART:20261004T130000
DTEND:20261004T150000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:4b2b4d27f82fb7b63828d6e70c00e7@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by the true story of Beverly’s beloved gray seal\, 
 Shoebert’s Unfinished Journey is a joyful new family operetta by Arpeggi
 one Ensemble. When Shoebert the seal found his way to a former mill pond\,
  he unexpectedly galumphed into the world of another Schubert—composer F
 ranz Schubert\, whose songs celebrate mills\, water\, and fish. In Arpeggi
 one’s heartwarming production\, Shoebert is a seal who loves music. As h
 e searches for his own song\, he encounters remarkable figures from the hi
 story of the North Shore’s shoe and textile industries\, from inventor J
 an Matzeliger to artist Virginia Lee Burton. Along the way\, he discovers 
 not only a song\, but a place to belong. Featuring two extraordinary singe
 r-storytellers\, live chamber music on period instruments\, and original w
 atercolor illustrations\, this charming production celebrates Beverly’s 
 past and present with humor\, heart\, and imagination. Created as part of 
 Beverly 400+\, Shoebert’s Unfinished Journey is a delightful experience 
 for children\, families\, and anyone who loves a good story. The operetta 
 has been developed in collaboration with the Beverly community\, including
  the Beverly Council on Aging\, Northshore Education Consortium\, Ayers El
 ementary School\, and children who helped create artwork at Arts Fest Beve
 rly. This program is funded in part by a grant from the Beverly Cultural C
 ouncil\, a local agency which is supported by Mass Cultural Council\, a st
 ate agency\; by a grant from the Mass Cultural Council\; and by the genero
 sity of many individual donors. Story and illustrations by Andrea LeBlanc 
 Music arranged by Thomas Carroll Aurora Martin\, soprano and narrator Dani
 el Fridley\, bass and narrator Andrea LeBlanc\, flute Thomas Carroll\, cla
 rinet Emily Hale\, violin Anna Seda\, cello April Sun\, piano\n\nSources: 
 North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/shoeberts-unf
 inished-journey/2026-10-04/1/
LOCATION:Off Cabot Comedy &#038\; Events\, 9 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA
 \, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/shoeberts-unfinished-journey/2026-10-0
 4/1/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Siqing Lu Violin Recital
DTSTART:20261004T000000
DTEND:20261004T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:644a0c16cc6962a48c318c34f97f39@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America’s 250th anniversary with an extraordinary 
 evening of music at one of Boston’s most historic landmarks. On October 
 4\, 2026\, internationally acclaimed violinist Siqing Lu joins pianist Der
 ek Wang at Faneuil Hall for East Meets West: From Mozart and Beethoven to 
 The Butterfly Lovers\, a special recital bringing together masterpieces of
  Western classical music and one of China’s most beloved musical works. 
 The program begins with Mozart’s elegant Violin Sonata No. 10 in B-flat 
 Major\, K. 378\, followed by Beethoven’s dramatic Violin Sonata No. 7 in
  C Minor\, Op. 30\, No. 2. The second half features a complete performance
  of The Butterfly Lovers Violin Concerto\, the celebrated Chinese work ins
 pired by the legendary story of Liang Shanbo and Zhu Yingtai. Siqing Lu is
  the first Asian violinist to win First Prize at Italy’s prestigious Pag
 anini International Violin Competition. He has performed in more than 40 c
 ountries and at renowned venues including Lincoln Center\, Vienna’s Musi
 kverein\, London’s Royal Opera House\, and the National Centre for the P
 erforming Arts in Beijing. Presented at Faneuil Hall—Boston’s historic
  “Cradle of Liberty”—the concert marks America’s 250th anniversary
  through a musical dialogue across cultures\, generations\, and traditions
 . LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://ww
 w.meetboston.com/event/siqing-lu-violin-recital/92595/
LOCATION:Faneuil Hall\, Faneuil Hall 4 South Market Street\, Boston\, MA\,
  02109
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/siqing-lu-violin-recital/92595/
END:VEVENT
