BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Rest is Politics US - The Battle for America: Midterms Tour 20
 26
DTSTART:20261005T000000
DTEND:20261005T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:27e715cf61bbb1c4e53df2fcdeca87@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by Anthony Scaramucci - former White House Director of 
 Communications\, Wall Street financier and founder of SkyBridge Capital an
 d Katty Kay\, the award-winning broadcaster and BBC US Special Corresponde
 nt\, The Rest Is Politics: US takes listeners inside the inner circles of 
 the White House and Washington power. Drawing on Anthony’s first-hand ex
 perience at the heart of American politics and Katty’s nearly 30 years c
 overing the United States\, the show goes beyond the headlines to unpack t
 he personalities\, policy battles and cultural forces shaping America’s 
 future. From presidential campaigns and foreign policy flashpoints to the 
 realities of life inside Trump’s White House\, The Rest Is Politics: US 
 offers sharp\, informed and accessible analysis of the world’s most powe
 rful country and the impact its politics has on the global stage.\n\nSourc
 es: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-rest-is-
 politics-us-the-battle-for-america%3a-midterms-tour-2026/90459/
LOCATION:The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02116
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-rest-is-politics-us-the-battle-fo
 r-america%3a-midterms-tour-2026/90459/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vault to Vessel: Explore "Old Ironsides"
DTSTART:20261005T000000
DTEND:20261005T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:bbe7255ac3916d1a6b840ac9349a87@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join USS Constitution Museum Curatorial Staff for a special vi
 ewing of artifacts in the Museum’s Samuel Eliot Morison Memorial Library
 \, followed by a guided tour of “Old Ironsides.” This exclusive\, guid
 ed exploration of naval life during the Age of Sail will start in the Muse
 um’s Reading Room to “open the vault” and look at items from the col
 lection. Then\, we’ll head over to board USS Constitution and journey th
 rough the decks to see how sailors lived and worked there in the early 180
 0s. Tickets are limited to fifteen (15) guests to enable interaction and a
  special experience. Tickets include a complimentary copy of Exploring Old
  Ironsides\, a visual souvenir guide created by the USS Constitution Museu
 m. Please note: USS Constitution is an active-duty U.S. Navy vessel. Atten
 dees 18+ will need a federal or state-issued photo ID for access to the sh
 ip. Access to USS Constitution is limited to visitors who can safely board
  the ship’s top (spar) deck via ramp unassisted. Wheelchairs are only al
 lowed to board during favorable tide conditions as the ramp can become too
  steep\; otherwise\, wheelchairs\, walkers\, scooters\, and strollers are 
 not allowed on board and must be left on the pier while touring the ship. 
 Access to the below decks requires climbing and descending steep ladder-li
 ke steps. 100% of the ticket proceeds support the efforts of the USS Const
 itution Museum\, a private\, non-profit organization. LEARN MORE / GET TIC
 KETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event
 /vault-to-vessel%3a-explore-old-ironsides/92951/
LOCATION:USS Constitution Museum\, Charlestown Navy Yard\, Boston\, MA\, 0
 2129
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/vault-to-vessel%3a-explore-old-ironsi
 des/92951/
END:VEVENT
