DESCRIPTION:Peter Marks of The Washington Post exclaims\, "It's UNFAIR to 
 make me laugh this much! SPAMALOT is a tightly packed clown car speeding t
 o musical theater nirvana!” SPAMALOT \, which first galloped onto Broadw
 ay in 2005\, features a book & lyrics by Eric Idle and music by John Du Pr
 ez and Eric Idle. The original Broadway production was nominated for fourt
 een Tony Awards and won three\, including Best Musical. The musical comedy
  lovingly ripped off from the film classic\, Monty Python and the Holy Gra
 il\, has everything that makes a great knight at the theatre\, from flying
  cows to killer rabbits\, British royalty to French taunters\, dancing gir
 ls\, rubbery shrubbery\, and of course\, the Lady of the Lake. SPAMALOT fe
 atures well-known song titles such as “Always Look on the Bright Side of
  Life\,” “The Song That Goes Like This\,” “Find Your Grail” and 
 more that have become beloved classics in the musical theatre canon. LEARN
  MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetb
 oston.com/event/monty-pythons-spamalot/91651/
