BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Taste the Teas That Steeped a Revolution
DTSTART:20261006T000000
DTEND:20261006T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:829654d8de27e1d27c6c6d8e4180b7@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The ritual of tea was just as important in colonial American l
 ife as it was in Great Britain. In the late 1700s\, acts of rebellion were
  planned over pots of the drink\, which led to the dumping of tea into Bos
 ton Harbor in 1773 and eventually to a revolution. Join author and tea his
 torian Bruce Richardson for an illustrated presentation about Boston's his
 toric tea culture and the East India Company leaves that sparked the War o
 f Independence. Following the talk\, participants will be able to taste th
 ree colonial-era teas\, (and accompanying snacks) and Richardson will be a
 vailable to sign copies of his book\, A Social History of Tea . Limited co
 pies of the book will be available for purchase at the Gift Store. This sp
 ecial evening celebrates our temporary exhibit\, Declaring the Revolution:
  America's Printed Path to Independence\, showcasing rare items from the D
 avid M. Rubenstein Americana Collection. Advanced registration is required
  and all guests under the age of 18 are required to have an adult chaperon
 e. This ticket does not include daytime general admission. Please purchase
  an additional general admission ticket if you would like to visit during 
 our normal operating hours. 10am-5pm The John F. Kennedy Presidential Libr
 ary and Museum exhibits will be open free of charge from 5:30 p.m. – 7:0
 0 p.m. Food and drink options will be available for purchase in the Cafe\,
  and our Museum Store will be open until 7:00 pm. *Please note that this p
 rogram is in-person only\, and will not be livestreamed. LEARN MORE / BUY 
 TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/ev
 ent/taste-the-teas-that-steeped-a-revolution/92812/
LOCATION:John F. Kennedy Presidential Library & Museum\, Columbia Point\, 
 Boston\, MA\, 02125
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/taste-the-teas-that-steeped-a-revolut
 ion/92812/
END:VEVENT
