BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Odyssey Opera Resurrects Boston Classicists
DTSTART:20261010T000000
DTEND:20261010T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:148096c33c3d1181ca09a8f4403fc6@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Odyssey Opera brings together three landmark works by the Bost
 on School composers: George W. Chadwick’s The Padrone\, a sharply drawn 
 portrait of immigrant life in turn‑of‑the‑century Boston\; Amy Beach
 ’s Jephthah’s Daughter\, a concentrated and moving retelling of the bi
 blical story\; and Edward MacDowell’s Laima\, a dramatic scene shaped by
  Lithuanian myth. Heard together\, these works illuminate the range and am
 bition of the composers who defined Boston’s early musical identity and 
 helped establish a distinctly American operatic voice.\n\nSources: Meet Bo
 ston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/odyssey-opera-resurrect
 s-boston-classicists/93197/
LOCATION:New England Conservatory\, 30 Gainsborough Street\, Boston\, MA\,
  02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/odyssey-opera-resurrects-boston-class
 icists/93197/
END:VEVENT
