  Hockney (1937–2026)‍
DTSTART:20261011T130000
DTEND:20261011T170000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:ffdd69d2c3581caf0791492f4d29b3@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Hockney Reproduction(s) is an exhibition that has been decades
  in the making. The Manship Barn Studio has been transformed by an amazing
  collection and selection of David Hockney’s printed exhibition posters
 \, faxes\, books\, photographs\, and more. The show is an unprecedented an
 d unparalleled homage to the artist\, and it is the final show that he app
 roved before his passing in June. Producer and curator of the show\, Bing 
 McGilvray\, said knowingly\, “David would have loved the show. And loved
  the place too\, an artists residency….” In the making for over a year
 \, the show exceeds expectations and should not be missed. REGISTRATION RE
 QUIRED.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org
 /event/hockney-reproductions-a-celebration-of-the-life-and-art-of-david-ho
 ckney-1937-2026/2026-10-11/
LOCATION:Manship Artists Residency\, P.O. Box 7071\, Gloucester\, MA\, 019
 30
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/hockney-reproductions-a-celebration-of
 -the-life-and-art-of-david-hockney-1937-2026/2026-10-11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jimmy Tingle: The “Radical” Middle- Why Would a Comedian Run f
 or Office? Film Screening + QA
DTSTART:20261011T190000
DTEND:20261011T220000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:47aab112d134c8cc3ff519d5855462@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Film Screening + Q&A with Jimmy Tingle In this extremely relev
 ant and provocative film Jimmy Tingle chronicles his fascinating transitio
 n from a life as a seasoned comedian featuring timeless clips from his set
  on the Tonight Show with Johnny Carson to his prescient commentary on Don
 ald Trump while serving as a humorist for 60 Minutes II to his riveting ad
 dress at the Massachusetts Democratic Convention as a candidate for LT Gov
 ernor. During the Q & A talk back Jimmy will continue to demonstrate his d
 istinctive brand of humor\, passion and creativity to lift our spirits out
  of the theatre\, into the streets and on to the polls. Quotes and Reviews
 : “Martin Luther King\, Jr.\, Winston Churchill\, and Jimmy Tingle all s
 poke on the Sanders Theatre stage at Harvard University\, and I can guaran
 tee you Jimmy Tingle got the most laughs… … gets my vote for Best Poli
 tical Comedy film of the Year.” – Paula Poundstone\, comedian “Gover
 nment Matters! That’s why a comedian runs for office. Jimmy Tingle\, wit
 h humor and cracking wit\, uses common sense to protect the common good fr
 om those who would tear down its essential political structures. No Joke. 
 This is Tingle at his best.” – James Carroll\, Author\, columnist Bost
 on Globe “Excellent! Hilarious! Very meaningful and laugh-out-loud funny
 !” – Steven Wright\, comedian\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page:
  https://northofboston.org/event/jimmy-tingle-the-radical-middle-why-would
 -a-comedian-run-for-office-film-screening-qa/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/jimmy-tingle-the-radical-middle-why-wo
 uld-a-comedian-run-for-office-film-screening-qa/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261011T110000
DTEND:20261011T170000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:55e5ea78dd03ea897899f5d15ecede@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-10-11/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-10-11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
