DESCRIPTION:Waves of Change Cape Cod Arts Festival returns for its second 
 year\, October 15 and 16\, 2026. Presented by the Social and Economic Just
 ice Institute at Cape Cod Community College\, the festival brings together
  a dynamic range of visual and performing artists\, cultural practitioners
 \, filmmakers\, writers\, and thought leaders to address how the arts addr
 ess social justice issues and create a thriving\, sustainable community. T
 his year the festival offerings range from hip hop Shakespeare and labor m
 ovement zine workshops to a community co-created mural project\; dance cla
 sses to a poetry “write-out” in conjunction with Barnstable Land Trust
 . Look for the signature social justice film fest on Thursday as well as t
 he live music extravaganza showcasing the acclaimed production\, Women ROC
 K! This year the festival culminates in a special collaborative event comb
 ining the Waves of Change closing party with Cape Cod Young Professionals
 ’ famed annual Bash. Check out the full schedule for a complete listing 
 of all the exciting activities this year’s festival offers. Come celebra
 te community\, social justice\, and the arts with us!\n\nSources: Cape Cod
