BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chelsea Berry
DTSTART:20261017T190000
DTEND:20261017T220000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:13a8c5e2384703d23c6dcfedf626fc@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Doors 6:30pm Show 7:00pm ALL AGES Premium Seating with cocktai
 l service: $44.50 + $6.95 service fee Standard Seating with cocktail servi
 ce: $34.50 – $39.50 + $6.95 service fee GA Standing: $29.50 + $6.95 serv
 ice fee + $5 Day of Show Chelsea Berry is a Maine-based indie singer songw
 riter known for her powerhouse vocals\, heartfelt songwriting\, and comman
 ding stage presence. Acclaimed artist Susan Werner once dubbed her “the 
 Pink of folk music”—a nod to Berry’s genre-blending style\, emotiona
 l depth\, and vibrant live energy. Over a 25-year career that includes thi
 rteen original albums\, Berry has built a loyal following all over the cou
 ntry. This October\, she returns to her former home on Cape Ann to celebra
 te the release of her newest album\, Peace Soldier. Recorded with engineer
  and co-producer Rich Lamb in Queens NYC\, with overdubs by engineer Warre
 n Babson at Bang-A-Song Studios in Gloucester\, Peace Soldier is a collabo
 rative\, cinematic\, rock-meets-musical-theater production built on empath
 y\, connection\, compassion\, and community\, while showcasing Berry’s p
 owerful and dynamic vocals\, innovative spirit\, and penchant for bringing
  people together. The songs of Peace Soldier and the message they carry wi
 ll resonate with listeners in a vastly deep and meaningful way. In this re
 lease performance\, the audience can expect to be confronted with question
 s\, ideas\, and collaborative insights centered on humanity\, common groun
 d\, war\, death\, love\, and the desire for peace. These themes are set wi
 thin a story arc of songs supported by far more dynamic and complex arrang
 ements than any in Berry’s past works. This special release performance 
 will feature her full band plus a cast of guest vocalists. Berry has appea
 red in Boston publications such as The Noise and Northshore Magazine\, and
  is regularly featured on Sirius XM as well as local radio stations across
  the country. Known for drawing audiences in “like moths to a flame\,”
  Berry continues to be a favorite among listening rooms nationwide. A vete
 ran of the road\, Berry has toured coast to coast and recorded albums in B
 oston\, New York\, Nashville\, and Denver. She has shared the stage with l
 egendary artists such as Livingston Taylor\, Chris Smither\, Mavis Staples
 \, Chris Isaak\, Shawn Colvin\, and many more. Originally from Alaska\, Ch
 elsea now makes her home just north of Acadia National Park in coastal Mai
 ne.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/eve
 nt/chelsea-berry-2/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/chelsea-berry-2/
END:VEVENT
