BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261017T110000
DTEND:20261017T170000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:62d645b3ccd5dd83818ae886721dcb@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-10-17/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-10-17/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Putting Science on the Map" with Cartographer Greg Fiske
DTSTART:20261017T000000
DTEND:20261017T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:abb04cf68f9a581487b1828d03ac66@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Maps can distill a story out of complex information and spark 
 conversation. In the stages of science\, there’s a continuum of map solu
 tions that aid in both the understanding of complex topics and the ability
  to reach broad audiences. From using participant-led mapping with Arctic 
 Indigenous communities to creating maps of climate change impacts for a gl
 obal audience\, the possibilities of maps in the realm of our science are 
 endless. Join Greg for an exploration of commonly used tools and technique
 s for making beautiful maps\, as well as common challenges\, success stori
 es\, and failures\, faced in nearly two and half decades of making maps fo
 r Woodwell Climate Research Center scientists. Mr. Fiske is the Director o
 f Geospatial Technology at Woodwell Climate Research Center in Woods Hole
 \, Massachusetts. As a geographer and cartographer\, he specializes in GIS
 \, remote sensing\, and data visualization. Fiske bridges art and science
 \, creating impactful maps to communicate complex climate data\, particula
 rly regarding Arctic ecosystems. The image attached is River Art. This ima
 ge shows elevation data from the ArcticDEM project (NGA-NSF) for the Lena 
 River delta region of north-central Siberia. The variations in pink shades
  indicate how water has changed the landscape through time. *You can view 
 more of Greg’s amazing work in his Naturescape Gallery exhibit\, Cartogr
 aphies of Arctic Change\, September through October. Naturescape Gallery i
 s in the Museum’s auditorium. Members: $20 / Non-Members $25 ~ Tickets a
 t CCMNH.org\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodc
 hamber.org/event/putting-science-on-the-map-with-cartographer-greg-fiske/5
 2476/
LOCATION:Cape Cod Museum of Natural History\, 869 Route 6A\, Brewster\, MA
 \, 02631
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/putting-science-on-the-map-with-c
 artographer-greg-fiske/52476/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rockport Harvest Fest 2026
DTSTART:20261017T110000
DTEND:20261017T170000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:ac892283d5ae2232f059e21a8beae6@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Harvest Fest FALL INTO FUN: HARVEST\, GATHER\, CELEBRATE! The 
 Greater Cape Ann Chamber of Commerce is excited to bring back this cherish
 ed community event! We invite you to join us by the shore for a unique ble
 nd of fall festivities and coastal charm\, where the crisp sea breeze meet
 s the warmth of community spirit. Come enjoy Rockport’s local charm and 
 bountiful harvest while you explore the scenic downtown and immerse yourse
 lf in festive seasonal activities. Whether you’re a longtime local or ju
 st visiting\, this is the perfect way to experience the magic of autumn by
  the sea. So\, grab your sweater and your loved ones\, and join us for a d
 ay of seaside celebration! Event Highlights Hometown Entertainment: Enjoy 
 live performances from local musicians and entertainers throughout the day
 . Local Vendors: Discover unique artisan goods and seasonal treats. Family
  Fun: Bring the kids and explore seasonal crafts\, face painting and a liv
 e animal exhibit! Seaside Bites and Brews: Savor seasonal favorites\, loca
 l cuisine and beer. Bake-Off: Come cheer on local bakers as they compete f
 or the title of Best Apple Pie! Shopping: Enjoy the rich artistic culture 
 and plentiful selections of our local retailers *Featured musical entertai
 nment from Headlands and Corey Wrinn Music *Apple Pie Bake Off – Come ch
 eer on amateur bakers as they compete for the title of best apple pie! Wan
 t to test your baking skills? Reach out to Colleen at colleen@capeannchamb
 er.com *Local craft beer from Rockport Brewing Co *Food provided by Meat &
  Sweet Foods and Rockport Brewing (more food vendors coming soon!)\, plus 
 don’t forget all the local favorite spots – whether your looking for a
  delicious lobster roll\, juicy burger or unforgettable donuts there’s s
 omething for everyone! *Various children’s activities throughout downtow
 n including live animal exhibit by Cape Ann Vernal Pond Team! *Lawn Games 
 at the First Congregational Church of Rockport *Shop to your hearts conten
 t! Browse through the offerings of several local vendors as well as the ma
 ny amazing shops throughout downtown Rockport 2026 Confirmed Vendors (more
  to come!) A&C Custom Creations Angela’s Creative Nook Cape Ann Sea Salt
  Edgewood Designs Greater Cape Ann Chamber of Commerce Hold Fast Company H
 ole in the Wall Care Kat’s Tales Nesting Threads Renuity (Silver Sponsor
 ) Rockport Candle Company Thacher & Straitsmouth Island Association The Ro
 oster’s Closet\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofb
 oston.org/event/rockport-harvest-fest-2026/
LOCATION:4 High Street\, 4 High Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/rockport-harvest-fest-2026/
END:VEVENT
