BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Talk with James E. Carroll: Murder on Cape Cod
DTSTART:20261021T000000
DTEND:20261021T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:63bc5c5461efd972204846775b97a6@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:We welcome Cape author and attorney James E. Carroll to the li
 brary on Wednesday\, October 21 at 4 p.m. Carroll is the author of the Jam
 ie Carson Legal Thriller Series (Reasonably Foreseeable\, Cross Examinatio
 n\, and the most recent Murder on Cape Cod)\, where intricate legal disput
 es\, relentless advocacy\, and unexpected twists keep readers turning page
 s. Each novel combines authentic courtroom drama with suspenseful storytel
 ling drawn from his decades of litigation experience. Join us as Jim discu
 sses his legal career and how he draws on his experience in his novel writ
 ing. Free and open to all. Part of the library’s Community Voices series
 . James E. Carroll is an attorney and an author of legal fiction. His Jami
 e Carson Legal Thriller Series opens a window into the world of high stake
 s litigation in federal and state courts practiced by only the best lawyer
 s. A Franklin\, Massachusetts native\, Jim is Jesuit educated at Boston Co
 llege High School and Fairfield University. After teaching in private and 
 public high schools\, Jim graduated cum laude as a member of the Law Revie
 w from Suffolk University Law School. He spent three years at a large Bost
 on law firm before joining the Office of Special Litigation as a Trial Att
 orney for the U.S. Department of Justice in Washington\, DC where he cut h
 is teeth trying numerous cases in federal court around the country to verd
 ict on behalf of the United States. Jim lives on Cape Cod and in Vero Beac
 h\, Florida. Register Here\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https
 ://www.capecodchamber.org/event/author-talk-with-james-e-carroll%3a-murder
 -on-cape-cod/52456/
LOCATION:West Falmouth Library\, 575 West Falmouth Highway\, West Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02574
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/author-talk-with-james-e-carroll%
 3a-murder-on-cape-cod/52456/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CAM Studio Art: Design and Print the Folly Cove Way
DTSTART:20261021T130000
DTEND:20261021T160000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:5daaed52f0819cf7256bc1e13f8107@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step into the spirit of the legendary Folly Cove Designers and
  learn the art of block printing with artist Mary Rhinelander in this four
 -week course. This class blends design fundamentals\, creative play\, and 
 the rich history of Cape Ann’s iconic design collective. Referencing her
  unpublished book\, Design and How\, you’ll explore the principles of de
 sign that Virginia Lee Demetrios taught her students—selecting a theme a
 nd exploring it deeply through clarity of line\, rhythm\, repetition\, and
  pattern—and you will discover how her timeless ideas can elevate your o
 wn artistic voice. Each week builds your confidence as you sketch\, carve
 \, and print your way towards an original finished artwork. Please note: T
 his class has four sessions. Mary Rhinelander is a professional artist wit
 h an MFA in printmaking. Gloucester is in her DNA\, starting with great-gr
 andparents who spent summers on Eastern Point. She lives in East Glouceste
 r\, in a yellow clapboard house once known as “The Summer Art House” w
 here painter Theresa Bernstein and her painter/printmaker husband\, Willia
 m Meyerowitz\, spent many decades (starting in 1924). Having purchased her
  home directly from their estate\, William’s etching press is still happ
 ily living in the sun-filled basement studio. Mary has had many solo and g
 roup shows and her work is in both public and private collections. She has
  painted murals\, designed logos and book covers\, illustrated for a varie
 ty of publications\, and taught students of all ages. In 2004 she founded 
 Mermade Press\, a fine art card business. With a deep affinity for the Fol
 ly Cove Designers and Virginia Lee Demetrios in particular\, it has been M
 ary’s great pleasure to bring block printing workshops into Cape Ann’s
  public schools with the support of CAM and the Gloucester Education Found
 ation.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/
 event/cam-studio-art-design-and-print-the-folly-cove-way/2026-10-21/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/cam-studio-art-design-and-print-the-fo
 lly-cove-way/2026-10-21/
END:VEVENT
