BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Falmouth Jazz Presents: Lucy Yeghiazaryan
DTSTART:20261023T000000
DTEND:20261023T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:28099a967d78718cf722da40241f96@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Lucy Yeghiazaryan is an American Armenian vocalist who brings 
 warmth\, elegance\, and emotional depth to the Great American Songbook. A 
 past finalist in the Thelonious Monk Competition\, Lucy has become a leadi
 ng voice in straight-ahead jazz by bringing the richness of her heritage t
 ogether with her love for the ultimate American artform. Growing up in pos
 t-Soviet Armenia\, she began listening to her father’s once-contraband c
 ollection of jazz records at a young age\, mimicking the sounds and styles
  of the likes of Ella and Sarah Vaughan before she even learned to speak E
 nglish. Lucy can be found performing in and outside of the US with regular
  appearances at Jazz at Lincoln Center\, Birdland\, Mezzrow\, Symphony Spa
 ce and more. We’re excited to welcome Lucy back to Falmouth\, accompanie
 d by Greg Ruggiero on guitar\, as part of this year’s Falmouth Jazz “W
 omen Who Lead” series.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https:/
 /www.capecodchamber.org/event/falmouth-jazz-presents%3a-lucy-yeghiazaryan/
 51966/
LOCATION:West Falmouth Library\, 41 Cachalot lane\, FALMOUTH\, MA\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/falmouth-jazz-presents%3a-lucy-ye
 ghiazaryan/51966/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Halloween on the Hill
DTSTART:20261023T173000
DTEND:20261023T203000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:d6a3416fb13fd3a86f2dde807c4c7e@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Visit Long Hill in Beverly\, MA for Halloween on the Hill! An 
 enchanting woodland hides an eerie graveyard\, haunted pirate ship\, styli
 sh scarecrows\, and thousands of hand-carved glowing jack-o’-lanterns. T
 he larger-than-life seasonal displays and family-friendly frights—expand
 ing and evolving every year—are perfect for all ages. Tickets are $27 fo
 r Adult Trustees Members/$32 for Adult Nonmembers/$27 for Members. $10 for
  Child Trustees Members/$15 for Child Nonmembers. Tickets are free for chi
 ldren under age 2. Select value nights offer tickets for $20 (members)/$25
  (nonmembers).\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofbos
 ton.org/event/halloween-on-the-hill/2026-10-23/
LOCATION:Long Hill\, 576 Essex Street\, Beverly\, MA 01915\, 576 Essex Str
 eet\, Beverly\, MA\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/halloween-on-the-hill/2026-10-23/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261023T110000
DTEND:20261023T170000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:3c0607aa7f9fb0af80e28522d1e116@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-10-23/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-10-23/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:PHANTOM
DTSTART:20261023T200000
DTEND:20261023T220000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:3e6e40f0aa08be2b1061e330c15654@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:PHANTOM\, the mesmerizing musical by Maury Yeston and Arthur K
 opit\, reimagines Gaston Leroux’s classic tale with soaring emotion and 
 unforgettable beauty. This lavish production combines an exquisitely craft
 ed story with a breathtaking score that has captivated audiences around th
 e world. Set beneath the Paris Opera House\, the story follows Erik\, a br
 illiant but tormented musical genius who lives in the catacombs\, and Chri
 stine\, a young singer whose extraordinary voice awakens his heart. As lov
 e\, jealousy\, and destiny intertwine\, Phantom reveals a more human and h
 eartbreaking side of the legendary figure. Filled with passion\, mystery\,
  and hauntingly beautiful music\, PHANTOM is musical theatre at its most t
 imeless and romantic.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nor
 thofboston.org/event/phantom/2026-10-23/
LOCATION:North Shore Music Theatre\, Dunham Road 54\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/phantom/2026-10-23/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Women Who Lead: Lucy Yeghiazaryan
DTSTART:20261023T000000
DTEND:20261023T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:777b437672557afcf95fcf881e5104@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Vocalist Lucy Yeghiazaryan joins our Women Who Lead series cel
 ebrating artistry\, individuality\, and voice. She brings warmth\, eleganc
 e\, and emotional depth to the Great American Songbook. A rising voice in 
 straight-ahead jazz\, she was a finalist in the Thelonious Monk Competitio
 n and has performed at leading venues including Jazz at Lincoln Center and
  Birdland. This is Lucy’s second appearance in our series. This concert 
 is co-sponsored by Falmouth Jazz and West Falmouth Library.\n\nSources: Ca
 pe Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/women-who
 -lead%3a-lucy-yeghiazaryan/51634/
LOCATION:West Falmouth Library\, 41 Cachalot lane\, FALMOUTH\, MA\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/women-who-lead%3a-lucy-yeghiazary
 an/51634/
