BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Woods Hole YOUTH Theater Company - Debut Performance SIX
DTSTART:20261024T000000
DTEND:20261025T000000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:de383b739de203009cc4f612c09ed4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Our queens have been absolutely killing it during rehearsals\,
  considering half of them got killed Don’t miss out on getting your roya
 l invite for the debut show of the Woods Hole Youth Theater Company now\, 
 tickets can be purchased at woodsholetheater.org SIX: TEEN EDITION is a fu
 ll-length adaptation of Toby Marlow and Lucy Moss’ international phenome
 non SIX\, modified for performance by teen actors for family audiences. Di
 vorced\, beheaded\, died\, divorced\, beheaded\, survived. From Tudor Quee
 ns to Pop Icons\, the SIX wives of Henry VIII take the mic to remix five h
 undred years of historical heartbreak into a Euphoric Celebration of 21st-
 century girl power! This new original musical is the global sensation that
  everyone is losing their head over. SIX made its world premiere at the Ed
 inburgh Fringe Festival in 2017\, presented by Cambridge University Musica
 l Theatre Society. October 15 & 16 at 7:00PM October 17 at 2:00PM October 
 22 & 23 at 7:00PM October 24 & 25 at 2:00PM\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\n
 Event page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/woods-hole-youth-theater-
 company-debut-performance-six/52544/
LOCATION:Woods Hole Theater Company\, 68 Water Street\, Woods Hole\, MA\, 
 02543
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/woods-hole-youth-theater-company-
 debut-performance-six/52544/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261024T111500
DTEND:20261024T161500
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:1c3704d9a46209c76df7bb0380836b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-10-24/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 0-24/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibition by Beverly Mitchell
DTSTART:20261025T150000
DTEND:20261025T170000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:8c45d0c0411df3e8aeb605310d51e1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Beverly Mitchell Art Exhibit at the GAR Memorial Library\, Wes
 t Newbury MA On Display Oct. 2-30\, 2026 during regular library hours Mond
 ay – Wednesday 10:00 AM — 7:00 PM Thursday – Friday 10:00 AM — 5:0
 0 PM Saturday 9:00 AM — 1:00 PM Opening Reception Oct. 2 from 3-5 pm Bev
 erly Mitchell is a graduate of the Montserrat College of Art in Beverly\, 
 MA. A longtime resident of West Newbury\, she has taught art classes at he
 r home studio at 4 Maple Street in West Newbury from 1990-2019\, starting 
 back up in 2022 post-Covid. She is still taking on art students of all age
 s. Beverly’s colorful art has been exhibited widely throughout the regio
 n. If you are interested in purchasing her art or in taking art classes\, 
 please call her at 978-363-2729.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: 
 https://northofboston.org/event/art-exhibition-by-beverly-mitchell/2026-10
 -25/
LOCATION:GAR Memorial Library\, 190 Main St.\, West Newbury\, MA\, 01985
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/art-exhibition-by-beverly-mitchell/202
 6-10-25/
END:VEVENT
