BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BT ALC Big Band
DTSTART:20261121T200000
DTEND:20261121T220000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:d5f853b22e49bfce6ed3f1aa5f3f46@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:BT ALC Big Band is excited to return to the Northshore to make
  their debut at The Cut Live! Since the group’s formation in 2010\, BT A
 LC Big Band\, led by trombonist Brian Thomas and trumpeter Alex Lee-Clark
 \, have gained a reputation for hard grooving original compositions featur
 ing the most talented jazz and funk musicians in Boston and beyond. BT ALC
  Big Band draws from the big band traditions of Duke Ellington\, Count Bas
 ie\, and Thad Jones and infuses music from funk legends like James Brown\,
  Parliament Funkadelic\, and The Meters\, creating an undeniably unique so
 und\, Big Band Funk.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nort
 hofboston.org/event/bt-alc-big-band/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/bt-alc-big-band/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ekep Nkwelle
DTSTART:20261121T193000
DTEND:20261121T213000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:46ea431cd66477760e07ff2395da48@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Ekep Nkwelle is a force in today’s jazz scene\, with a journ
 ey from Washington\, DC\, to New York City. She refined her talents at Duk
 e Ellington School of the Arts\, Howard University\, and The Juilliard Sch
 ool. “Nkwelle is a rising star of her own.” –All About Jazz Her capt
 ivating voice has earned her collaborations with jazz legends like Wynton 
 Marsalis\, Dianne Reeves\, Dee Dee Bridgewater\, Cyrus Chestnut\, and the 
 late Russell Malone. She has also performed on renowned stages including S
 FJAZZ\, NPR’s Tiny Desk Concert\, Marians Jazzroom\, and the Umbria Jazz
  Festival. In 2023\, she received the Juilliard Career Advancement Grant\,
  nominated by Marsalis\, highlighting her artistry. Beyond performing\, Ek
 ep supports influential arts organizations including The National Jazz Mus
 eum in Harlem and Jazz Houston\, and she is one of Jazz at Lincoln Center
 ’s latest rising stars.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https:/
