BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261217T111500
DTEND:20261217T161500
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:18a7111fced84016d9313e8f40e308@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-12-17/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 2-17/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BrassFed Nation’s Holiday Bash
DTSTART:20261218T200000
DTEND:20261218T220000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:66cd4485edfd984bcf8e77a6b6adbd@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Doors 7:00pm Show 8:00pm ALL AGES Premium Seating with cocktai
 l service: $39.50 + $6.95 service fee Standard Seating with cocktail servi
 ce: $29.50 – $34.50 + $6.95 service fee Rear Floor Seating: $24.50 + $6.
 95 service fee GA Standing: $19.50 + $6.95 service fee ($10 Student Ticket
 s) + $5 Day of Show Carlos Menezes Jr’s BrassFed Nation is a horn-driven
  groove machine with a unique sound incorporating the styles and tradition
 s of early Jazz\, New Orleans Funk & Soul\, Rhythm & Blues\, Calypso\, and
  Jamaican Ska! Founded in 2013\, The BrassFed Nation is dedicated to the a
 dvancement of horn-driven music through exposure and outreach in both educ
 ation and local musical culture! The collective features 3 unique ensemble
 s\; Cape Ann Big Band\, The Jambalaya Horns\, and The 13-Piece DubTone Orc
 hestra – all striving to inspire and connect musicians of all ages throu
 gh performances\, private studio lessons\, workshops\, and interactive cli
 nics. ABOUT THIS PERFORMANCE: Paying homage to the infectious beats and so
 unds of New Orleans and the Caribbean\, the BrassFed Orchestra will cue th
 e “Big Four” and transport audience members to the streets of the Cres
 cent City for a Holiday Celebration that is full of surprises! This year
 ’s program will showcase members of The Jambalaya Horns and feature a nu
 mber of guest instrumentalists from the New England music scene! Featured 
 Vocalists are Jacyn Tremblay\, Rhiannon Hurst\, and Alessandro Schoc. WEBS
 ITE: www.brassfednation.com ABOUT JACYN TREMBLAY: Jacyn Tremblay is a Bost
 on based singer\, songwriter\, and recording artist known for her dynamic 
 vocals and versatile artistry! Recent performances include singing with th
 e Boston Pops\, The Plymouth Phil\, and several other regional orchestras
 \, co-producing the female vocal tribute show MUSE: A Salute to Divas of t
 he 90’s (@musedivas)\, and has original music with the pop trio Three Se
 cond Chances (@threesecondchances). When she’s not working with the musi
 c non-profit Music Drives Us\, she’s singing every weekend with several 
 of New England’s leading event bands on the Wilson Stevens Agency. You c
 an hear her voice on TV and radio for NBC Boston\, WBZ Radio\, Boston 25\,
  WGBH and more! Jacyn is excited to sing with Carlos and the amazing music
 ians of BFN! For more upcoming performances and fun follow her @Jacynthegi
 rl or visit jacyntremblaymusic.com ABOUT RHIANNON HURST: Award-winning jaz
 z vocalist Rhiannon Kaela Hurst has earned recognition on both national an
 d international stages. With an unwavering passion for music\, she perform
 s regularly with big bands and combos across New England. Rhiannon was nam
 ed a 2021 Award Winner in the Jazz Voice category of the prestigious Natio
 nal YoungArts Competition. She was a featured artist at the 2023 Internati
 onal Guinness Jazz Festival in Ireland\, performing as a solo artist and a
 s an opener. Rhiannon graduated from the College of the Holy Cross as the 
 2025 Brooks Music Scholar and Fenwick Scholar\, completing her undergradua
 te studies in conjunction with jazz voice training at the New England Cons
 ervatory of Music with Professor Dominique Eade. She recently graduated fr
 om NEC\, with a Master’s in Jazz Vocal Performance as the inaugural stud
 ent in the 4+1 program between Holy Cross and New England Conservatory. AB
 OUT ALESSANDRO SCHOC: Alessandro is a vocalist and live performer dedicate
 d to the stage. With a musical identity shaped by artists such as Lewis Ca
 paldi\, Bruno Mars and Teddy Swims\, Alessandro is able to captivate any a
 udience he comes across. He approaches every performance as a unique exper
 ience singing with passion and joy in every word. Whether it be an emotion
 al ballad or a high energy groove\, his dynamic vocal range and passionate
  stage presence is sure to leave a lasting impression.\n\nSources: North o
 f Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/brassfed-nations-hol
 iday-bash/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/brassfed-nations-holiday-bash/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Captain Elias Davis House Tour
DTSTART:20261218T140000
DTEND:20261218T143000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:bc282fed438ea016bece4028707d2a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:What can a house tell us about the people who lived there? Ste
 p inside the Capt. Elias Davis House and discover how architecture\, craft
 smanship\, and everyday objects reveal the lives of one Gloucester family 
 and the changing history of Cape Ann. This docent-led experience invites v
 isitors to look closely at the details that transform a historic building 
 into a story of community\, commerce\, and home.\n\nSources: North of Bost
 on\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/captain-elias-davis-house-
 tour/2026-12-18/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/captain-elias-davis-house-tour/2026-12
 -18/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Good Winter with Seamus Egan
DTSTART:20261218T193000
DTEND:20261218T213000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:24c8905c9186a7c6341a9455729ed6@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the warmth\, wonder\, and storytelling spirit of the
  season with Good Winter: A Celtic Christmas. Acclaimed musician and compo
 ser Seamus Egan invites audiences on a richly woven holiday journey of mus
 ic\, song\, poetry\, and story\, drawing on Celtic traditions that honor c
 ommunity\, memory\, and the turning of the year. Blending beloved seasonal
  songs\, original works\, traditional tunes\, and spoken word\, this intim
 ate and uplifting program captures the joy\, humor\, and reflection that d
 efine the holiday season. From his beginnings as a teen prodigy\, to his g
 roundbreaking solo work with Shanachie Records\, to founding the influenti
 al Irish-American band Solas\, Seamus Egan has inspired generations of mus
 icians and helped shape the sound of contemporary Irish music. His work as
  a film composer and musical director has deepened his understanding of mu
 sic’s power to tell stories\, and nowhere is that gift more evident than
  in Good Winter. Featuring fiddle\, flute\, whistle\, guitar\, banjo\, pia
 no\, accordion\, and vocals\, Egan and his ensemble create an atmosphere t
 hat is both celebratory and deeply personal. Filled with soaring melodies
 \, heartfelt stories\, and festive spirit\, Good Winter: A Celtic Christma
 s is a joyous invitation to gather together\, reflect on the year gone by
 \, and welcome the season with warmth and song.\n\nSources: North of Bosto
 n\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/good-winter-with-seamus-ega
 n/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/good-winter-with-seamus-egan/
END:VEVENT
