BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homeschool Scholars: Seasonal Rhythms
DTSTART:20270114T090000
DTEND:20270114T120000
DTSTAMP:20261004T161355Z
UID:cad4101945435a3e1f9e38ceb99a17@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us in October for weekly homeschool programs exploring th
 e seasonal rhythms of the trails\, woodlands\, farm fields\, and coastline
 s of the Crane Estate and Appleton Farms! October is a great time to see h
 ow nature is changing and getting ready for winter. Participants will expl
 ore the coastline\, trails\, and woodlands of The Crane Estate & Appleton 
 Farms\, while making observations\, taking measurements\, and learning how
  scientists study nature as the seasons change. This is a drop-off program
  that is open to ages 5-11 and will include small group work specialized a
 ctivities based on age and peer mentoring opportunities between age groups
 . The class takes place rain or shine\, with as much time spent outdoors a
 s possible. Students should arrive dressed for the weather and bring a lun
 ch and water bottle. Homeschool Scholars: Seasonal Rhythms- This 4-class s
 eries program takes place on Thursdays from 9am-12pm on October 1\, 8\, 15
 \, & 22. Crane Estate: October 1 & 15 Appleton Farms: October 8 & 22 Tuiti
 on for the 4 classes is $275 for Trustees Members and $325 for nonmembers.
  Registration covers all listed session dates.\n\nSources: North of Boston
 \nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-scholars-seasonal
 -rhythms/2027-01-14/
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-scholars-seasonal-rhythms/2
 027-01-14/
END:VEVENT
